{title: O Day of Peace That Dimly Shines}
{key: C}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Tune: Jerusalem}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O [C]day of [Am]peace that [F]dimly [C]shines
[F]Through all our [C]hopes and [Dm]prayers and [F]dreams
Guide [C]us to [Am]justice, [Em]truth, and [Am]love
De[Em]livered [Am]from our [Em]sel[D]fish [G]schemes
May [G]swords of [Dm]hate fall [Gm]from our [Dm]hands
Our hearts from [F]envy [Bb]find re[F]lease
Till by God's [Dm]grace our [G]warring [C]world
Shall [Am]see Christ's [F]promised [C]reign [G]of [C]peace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Then [C]shall the [Am]wolf dwell [F]with the [C]lambs
[F]Nor shall the [C]fierce de[Dm]vour the [F]small
As [C]beasts and [Am]cattle [Em]calmly [Am]graze
A [Em]little [Am]child shall [Em]lead [D]them [G]all
Then [G]ene[Dm]mies shall [Gm]learn to [Dm]love
All creatures [F]find their [Bb]true ac[F]cord
The hope of [Dm]peace shall [G]be ful[C]filled
For [Am]all the [F]earth shall [C]know [G]the [C]Lord.
{end_of_verse}
